1
00:02:30,016 --> 00:02:59,996
We'll be right back.

2
00:03:00,016 --> 00:03:29,996
We'll be right back.

3
00:03:30,016 --> 00:03:59,996
We'll be right back.

4
00:04:00,016 --> 00:04:02,616
Come back, Robin.

5
00:04:03,136 --> 00:04:04,836
Showdown with CP9.

6
00:04:10,016 --> 00:04:10,976
Oh, yeah.

7
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:14,396
Those are the same guys that were with you back at the shipyard, right?

8
00:04:14,816 --> 00:04:15,156
Right?

9
00:04:16,156 --> 00:04:19,496
Actually, that square-nosed guy came to our ship.

10
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:20,216
I see.

11
00:04:20,796 --> 00:04:23,196
And the attack on Iceberg was an inside job.

12
00:04:23,716 --> 00:04:24,356
Wait, what?

13
00:04:24,396 --> 00:04:25,196
I don't get it.

14
00:04:25,196 --> 00:04:33,496
Paulie, in all honesty, we're secret agents working for the world government.

15
00:04:34,196 --> 00:04:37,316
But hey, you'll forgive me if I say I'm sorry, right?

16
00:04:38,396 --> 00:04:43,436
We were comrades, building ships together every day from dawn till dusk.

17
00:04:43,436 --> 00:04:50,536
I realize this is quite sudden for you, so perhaps you'd believe me if I smashed Iceberg's face.

18
00:04:50,536 --> 00:04:55,776
Just shut the hell up.

19
00:04:56,256 --> 00:04:57,276
I've heard enough.

20
00:04:58,136 --> 00:05:00,896
You were that guy in the bull mask, weren't you?

21
00:05:01,636 --> 00:05:04,336
That was the first time I ever heard your voice.

22
00:05:04,836 --> 00:05:07,836
All those years, you never said a word.

23
00:05:08,236 --> 00:05:10,356
But you can talk just fine.

24
00:05:10,356 --> 00:05:14,456
I'll teach you to make fun of me!

25
00:05:14,696 --> 00:05:15,956
Paulie, stop it!

26
00:05:17,356 --> 00:05:18,036
Pipe.

27
00:05:18,516 --> 00:05:19,116
Hitch.

28
00:05:19,636 --> 00:05:20,716
Knife!

29
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:26,436
Bring your pistol.

30
00:05:35,636 --> 00:05:38,796
You still haven't learned your lesson, have you?

31
00:05:40,356 --> 00:05:55,216
Hey, are you okay?

32
00:05:57,896 --> 00:05:59,256
Screw you.

33
00:06:01,636 --> 00:06:02,216
Lucci.

34
00:06:10,356 --> 00:06:14,816
It's pointless to resist.

35
00:06:15,376 --> 00:06:19,376
Our abilities far exceed those of a normal human, as you can see.

36
00:06:20,116 --> 00:06:23,776
After many years of training, we've mastered an art called the Six Powers.

37
00:06:24,236 --> 00:06:29,276
These techniques transform the body into a living weapon with the strength of over a hundred men.

38
00:06:29,276 --> 00:06:34,736
Cuckoo!

39
00:06:34,996 --> 00:06:36,276
Stop drinking, Paulie!

40
00:06:36,356 --> 00:06:37,516
What about all that debt?

41
00:06:37,576 --> 00:06:38,316
Come on!

42
00:06:38,456 --> 00:06:39,976
I want some cash today.

43
00:06:40,236 --> 00:06:41,636
Next round's on me, okay?

44
00:06:42,296 --> 00:06:43,396
Bring it, Bluno.

45
00:06:43,816 --> 00:06:44,636
Let's go!

46
00:06:45,016 --> 00:06:45,976
You got it.

47
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:55,076
Callie for you, Hussie!

48
00:06:55,236 --> 00:06:56,976
That skirt is way too short!

49
00:06:59,196 --> 00:07:01,016
Hey, give it a rest, Paulie.

50
00:07:01,136 --> 00:07:03,276
If you don't like it, don't look at her, okay?

51
00:07:03,276 --> 00:07:14,756
After all his time, why?

52
00:07:17,916 --> 00:07:19,416
Sorry, Paulie.

53
00:07:22,716 --> 00:07:24,456
Our friendship is over.

54
00:07:25,736 --> 00:07:27,716
I have to eliminate you.

55
00:07:29,056 --> 00:07:29,776
Lucci!

56
00:07:30,036 --> 00:07:30,916
No, don't!

57
00:07:30,916 --> 00:07:31,956
You jerk!

58
00:07:32,556 --> 00:07:33,916
Leave him alone!

59
00:07:44,636 --> 00:07:46,676
Gumsho entreg!

60
00:07:48,916 --> 00:07:50,596
I embody Godland!

61
00:07:54,356 --> 00:07:58,976
I embody Godland!

62
00:07:58,976 --> 00:08:05,416
What the? That didn't work at all.

63
00:08:11,496 --> 00:08:13,956
You're nothing but a pest, Shave.

64
00:08:15,176 --> 00:08:16,336
He's gone.

65
00:08:22,416 --> 00:08:23,656
Finger pistol.

66
00:08:28,976 --> 00:08:51,656
If you weren't made out of rubber, you'd be dead with a hole in your neck.

67
00:08:52,496 --> 00:08:53,296
Lucky you.

68
00:08:58,976 --> 00:09:14,896
You're protecting him. But why?

69
00:09:15,256 --> 00:09:17,936
Why not? Because I don't want you to kill him!

70
00:09:18,596 --> 00:09:22,176
You guys were all friends just the other day. How could you do this?

71
00:09:22,176 --> 00:09:29,316
We were. Now, things have changed.

72
00:09:29,996 --> 00:09:33,976
It doesn't matter. You can say what you want. You're a bunch of traitors.

73
00:09:34,816 --> 00:09:36,816
The point is, you're my enemy now.

74
00:09:37,656 --> 00:09:42,896
I made a promise with Polly to beat the crap out of anybody who tries to hurt Ice Pops.

75
00:09:42,896 --> 00:09:48,576
I see. You decided to trust him over us, huh?

76
00:09:48,876 --> 00:09:52,376
That's right. Because you guys took away one of my friends!

77
00:09:53,276 --> 00:09:56,476
Hey, Robin, what gives? Why are you acting like this?

78
00:09:57,036 --> 00:09:59,976
If you want to leave the crew, at least tell me why!

79
00:10:00,656 --> 00:10:05,276
Yeah, and why would you want to team up with people from the world government? That's crazy!

80
00:10:05,276 --> 00:10:17,656
Do I have to repeat myself? I believe I said my farewells to the cook and the doctor before I left.

81
00:10:18,236 --> 00:10:19,936
Didn't you pass that along, Chopper?

82
00:10:20,136 --> 00:10:25,396
Of course I did! But just because I heard it doesn't mean I accept it! How could you do this?

83
00:10:25,716 --> 00:10:30,856
I did it to make my wish come true. A wish that can't happen as long as we're together.

84
00:10:31,076 --> 00:10:32,996
And if you can't accept that, I'm sorry.

85
00:10:35,276 --> 00:10:51,236
You may not find it fair, but to accomplish my goal, I'll make any sacrifice.

86
00:10:52,516 --> 00:10:59,216
I see. And that includes framing your own crewmates for attempted murder. So what is this wish of yours?

87
00:10:59,436 --> 00:11:01,336
I don't have to answer that question.

88
00:11:01,336 --> 00:11:12,696
Are you out of your mind? Wake up, Robin. You have no right to do this. I don't care what it is you're trying to accomplish. The consequences are far too great.

89
00:11:12,956 --> 00:11:16,056
I've heard enough. This is no longer your choice to make.

90
00:11:17,556 --> 00:11:19,156
This should shut you up.

91
00:11:21,456 --> 00:11:23,056
No! Iceberg!

92
00:11:23,056 --> 00:11:28,296
I won't let anyone get in my way.

93
00:11:47,296 --> 00:11:49,776
I won't let anyone get in my way.

94
00:11:49,776 --> 00:11:57,896
Nothing you're saying is making any sense! You expect me to believe this?

95
00:11:59,136 --> 00:12:01,336
Robin! What happened to you?

96
00:12:07,076 --> 00:12:11,116
You're our friend, Rice! Please, Robin! Come back!

97
00:12:11,116 --> 00:12:17,836
Sorry to break up the reunion, but I'll have to stop you there.

98
00:12:19,636 --> 00:12:23,236
You see, we have a date this evening with a very important individual.

99
00:12:23,536 --> 00:12:25,436
One that's been over four years in the making.

100
00:12:25,836 --> 00:12:26,816
We're finished here.

101
00:12:27,476 --> 00:12:31,016
In other words, that means we're finished with you as well.

102
00:12:35,956 --> 00:12:38,016
Khalifa, how much time is left?

103
00:12:39,296 --> 00:12:40,216
Two minutes.

104
00:12:40,216 --> 00:12:43,516
Here's the deal.

105
00:12:44,116 --> 00:12:48,576
I know this is sudden, but in two minutes, this building will go up in a ball of flame.

106
00:12:51,456 --> 00:12:52,256
You're kidding!

107
00:12:52,836 --> 00:12:53,836
Of course not.

108
00:12:54,316 --> 00:12:57,676
Fire is an effective tool for erasing all sorts of evidence.

109
00:12:58,116 --> 00:13:02,316
If you don't want to be burned alive, I suggest you leave the building as soon as possible.

110
00:13:02,316 --> 00:13:04,616
Oh, well, I say that.

111
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:11,116
But I have no intention of letting you go.

112
00:13:16,616 --> 00:13:21,616
Looks like it's going to be us against them, and our friend Robin has clearly picked her side.

113
00:13:21,616 --> 00:13:25,916
Luffy, Robin is not one of us anymore.

114
00:13:25,916 --> 00:13:27,656
Do you accept that now?

115
00:13:32,076 --> 00:13:33,476
No! No way!

116
00:13:33,476 --> 00:13:36,936
So noisy.

117
00:13:36,936 --> 00:13:40,016
Anyway, the first floor is about to set fire.

118
00:13:40,216 --> 00:13:41,256
It won't be pretty.

119
00:13:41,876 --> 00:13:44,276
But to be fair, the culprits are just pirates.

120
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:46,896
You can't expect them to be subtle.

121
00:13:47,376 --> 00:13:48,396
You bastards!

122
00:13:48,396 --> 00:13:57,016
That's nice of you to give us credit for your attempted arson, but I think that I'll pass.

123
00:13:57,316 --> 00:14:00,676
What's one more crime when we're going to execute you anyway?

124
00:14:00,676 --> 00:14:10,176
Well, I suppose I'll take my leave now.

125
00:14:10,596 --> 00:14:12,476
You've done exactly as you were told.

126
00:14:12,976 --> 00:14:13,616
Good work.

127
00:14:14,396 --> 00:14:14,756
Robin!

128
00:14:15,016 --> 00:14:15,696
Don't go!

129
00:14:16,076 --> 00:14:17,436
You're still one of us!

130
00:14:18,036 --> 00:14:18,916
This is farewell.

131
00:14:20,096 --> 00:14:20,476
Robin!

132
00:14:24,216 --> 00:14:25,116
Stop her.

133
00:14:26,816 --> 00:14:27,816
Straw hat.

134
00:14:27,816 --> 00:14:31,316
We finally found you!

135
00:14:31,516 --> 00:14:33,456
I won't let you run away again!

136
00:14:33,836 --> 00:14:34,916
Out of my way!

137
00:14:35,276 --> 00:14:36,276
Iron body.

138
00:14:44,656 --> 00:14:45,136
Hmm.

139
00:14:46,536 --> 00:14:49,716
How come nothing I do to these guys even phases them?

140
00:14:50,196 --> 00:14:57,416
In addition to our offensive techniques, our training has also given us the ability to make our body as solid as an iron wall.

141
00:14:57,816 --> 00:15:01,356
Of course, your punches are weak to begin with.

142
00:15:01,516 --> 00:15:02,576
Okay, whatever!

143
00:15:02,976 --> 00:15:05,276
I said out of my way!

144
00:15:05,476 --> 00:15:06,676
Paper art.

145
00:15:06,676 --> 00:15:23,436
Even though he's big, he sure is fast!

146
00:15:23,436 --> 00:15:25,736
He's moving like his body's made of paper!

147
00:15:29,816 --> 00:15:30,796
Oh no!

148
00:15:31,256 --> 00:15:31,956
Robin!

149
00:15:31,956 --> 00:15:37,916
Move it!

150
00:15:37,916 --> 00:15:39,496
Come on!

151
00:15:39,496 --> 00:15:41,756
Pistol!

152
00:15:43,376 --> 00:15:43,956
Shave!

153
00:15:45,656 --> 00:15:46,936
He disappeared!

154
00:15:49,776 --> 00:15:54,116
My legs are so strong that I can move faster than your eyes can see.

155
00:15:55,376 --> 00:15:56,396
Stand still!

156
00:15:56,396 --> 00:15:57,396
Moon walk.

157
00:15:58,056 --> 00:16:01,736
In fact, I can even leap off of the air itself.

158
00:16:03,896 --> 00:16:04,736
He's flying!

159
00:16:07,936 --> 00:16:08,936
Tempest!

160
00:16:09,056 --> 00:16:09,556
Kick!

161
00:16:14,156 --> 00:16:15,356
A slashing attack?

162
00:16:15,736 --> 00:16:16,436
Get down!

163
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:17,476
Hurry!

164
00:16:17,856 --> 00:16:18,356
Why?

165
00:16:18,356 --> 00:16:19,356
Luffy!

166
00:16:19,356 --> 00:16:37,316
They did all that with a single kick?

167
00:16:37,436 --> 00:16:38,076
No way!

168
00:16:38,356 --> 00:16:41,496
Technically, it was the sharp gust of wind that followed it.

169
00:16:41,956 --> 00:16:43,996
We call it the tempest kick.

170
00:16:43,996 --> 00:16:53,116
We met on your ship.

171
00:16:53,116 --> 00:16:53,136
We met on your ship.

172
00:21:55,147 --> 00:22:06,747
疲れ果てた向きの中でも変わらないもの探すコンバスで いつまでも持っていれるから

173
00:22:06,747 --> 00:22:19,147
いつか辿り着く夢の終わりに できるだけこのままで大人に 見上げた果てしないこの大空に 永遠に 永遠に

174
00:22:19,147 --> 00:22:31,207
幼き頃の夢物語 忘られち記憶の糸辿り 未だ胸を焦がす残り火を消してしまわないように

175
00:22:31,207 --> 00:22:42,047
乱れた晴れ渡るこの空に 仲間と共に想いを託し 移り変わる時代を越え 永遠に 永遠に

176
00:22:49,147 --> 00:23:12,147
実際にとって 実際には大きめが大きい break ボシッシュのようだ

177
00:23:12,147 --> 00:23:13,427
King of the Pirates!

